{
  "name": "dawnlist-feed-worker",
  "main": "src/index.js",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-09-06",
  "observability": { "enabled": true },
  // The daily retention purge (src/retention.js). Once a day is enough: the
  // shortest period it enforces is two days.
  "triggers": { "crons": ["17 3 * * *"] },
  "d1_databases": [
    { "binding": "DB", "database_name": "dawnlist", "database_id": "8c272845-1e82-4660-ab71-01bef14c897e" }
  ],
  "vars": {
    // The LIVE Paddle price for the Standard plan, created 2026-09-08 on
    // product pro_01m217zsvqcexs9atdswvja3sf at $79/month recurring.
    //
    // Committed deliberately. A price id is a public identifier — it appears
    // in the checkout every customer sees — and keeping it in the repository
    // is what makes a mismatch findable. Hidden as a secret, nobody could
    // tell which id was configured when a customer landed on the wrong plan.
    //
    // Comma-separate when annual or per-currency ids are added.
    "PADDLE_PRICE_STANDARD": "pri_01m217zszynjmwmcx6xqpewxc1",

    // What /v1/apple requires every Apple purchase to be for. Public
    // identifiers, committed so a mismatch is findable: a wrong value refuses
    // every Mac subscriber with `wrong_bundle` or `wrong_product`.
    "APPLE_BUNDLE_ID": "com.spencerfields.dawnlist",
    "APPLE_PRODUCT_ID": "com.spencerfields.dawnlist.monthly",
    // Which App Store offers may be comped, by the NAME Apple puts in a
    // signed transaction as offerIdentifier. Comma-separated. A subscription
    // that began with one of these may be kept alive past Apple's free period
    // by an administrator; one that began any other way never can, which is
    // what stops a lapsed paying customer being comped by mistake.
    // Not a secret: it is a list of offer names, and it is here rather than in
    // code so a new comp tier is a config change and not a deploy of logic.
    "APPLE_COMP_OFFERS": "Dawnlist Comps",
    // The Microsoft Store add-on, as the collections API names it. Paddle
    // declined the Dawnlist domain on 2026-09-11 and an appeal is open, so
    // the Store sells its own subscription alongside rather than instead.
    "MS_PRODUCT_ID": "9P0THQRBKFPF"
    // MS_TENANT_ID, MS_CLIENT_ID and MS_CLIENT_SECRET are SECRETS and are
    // deliberately not here. Only the last is a secret in the cryptographic
    // sense; the other two are identifiers — but THIS REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC,
    // and a tenant id published in it names the directory to anyone looking
    // for one to phish. They cost nothing to hold as secrets, so all three go
    // in through `wrangler secret put`. See DAWNLIST-AZURE-AD-SETUP.md.
    //
    // MS_PRODUCT_ID stays above BECAUSE it is already public: it is the Store
    // ID printed on the listing page.

    // PADDLE_PRICE_GLOBAL is deliberately ABSENT. The Global plan is not sold
    // until its 2,500/day ceiling has been measured against a real
    // multi-region sweep — selling an untested allowance is how a cap quietly
    // becomes the thing that decides coverage.
  }
  // Secrets (wrangler secret put <NAME> — the command takes the secret's NAME,
  // never its value; the value goes at the interactive prompt only):
  //   THEIRSTACK_API_KEY      the feed credential. The ONLY place it lives.
  //   PADDLE_WEBHOOK_SECRET   separate signing key from EasyPost's
  //   CLIENT_HASH_SECRET      keys the HMAC stored in code_attempts in place of
  //                           the connecting address. Optional. Unset, a
  //                           SHA-256 with a salt fixed in src/codes.js is
  //                           stored instead: that still keeps addresses out
  //                           of the table, but anybody holding the source and
  //                           a copy of the table can hash candidate addresses
  //                           and match them. Set it to close that.

  //   APPLE_SHARED_SECRET     App-Specific Shared Secret; verifies the receipt
  //                           the Mac build in review sends
  //   APPLE_IAP_KEY_ID        In-App Purchase key id    } App Store Server API,
  //   APPLE_IAP_ISSUER_ID     issuer id                 } for builds that send
  //   APPLE_IAP_PRIVATE_KEY   the .p8 file's contents   } a transaction id
  // Unset, /v1/apple answers 503 `apple_not_configured`, which the app treats
  // as unreachable rather than as "not subscribed".
  //
  // ANTHROPIC_API_KEY was listed here and IS NOT USED. Nothing in src/ reads
  // it. It belonged to an inference proxy that was built and REMOVED on
  // 2026-09-06, because proxying job descriptions plus the fit brief and
  // factsheet would make Spencer a processor of every buyer's career record.
  // If that secret is still set on the deployed Worker, delete it —
  // `wrangler secret delete ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`. A credential kept for a
  // capability that was deliberately removed is pure exposure.
  //
  // Plain vars, NOT secrets (Paddle price ids are public identifiers, and
  // keeping them visible is what makes a misconfiguration findable):
  //   PADDLE_PRICE_STANDARD   comma-separated price ids for the Standard plan
  //   PADDLE_PRICE_GLOBAL     comma-separated price ids for the Global plan
  //
  // They are comma-separated because one plan legitimately has several price
  // ids — monthly and annual, and one per currency where Paddle issues
  // separate ids. Set them per environment: sandbox and production issue
  // DIFFERENT ids for the same product, and a purchase whose price id matches
  // nothing is acknowledged and issues NO licence (action `unmatched_product`,
  // price id logged), so a missing id here means a customer who paid and
  // received nothing until a code is minted for them in /admin.
  //
  // A plan is offered by /v1/plan only when its variable holds a price, so
  // leaving PADDLE_PRICE_GLOBAL unset is also what keeps Global off the
  // upgrade ladder.
}
